WEBVTT

00:10:57.692 --> 00:11:00.363
because that's how our culture
passes down moral lessons:

00:11:00.387 --> 00:11:02.355
we hire a bunch of very successful people

00:11:02.379 --> 00:11:04.669
to give speeches on why
success is not important.

00:11:04.693 --> 00:11:07.367
And they always tell you
you shouldn't be afraid to fail,

00:11:07.391 --> 00:11:10.188
from which you learn
if you’re JK Rowling, failure is fine,

00:11:10.212 --> 00:11:12.023
but for the rest of us, failure sucks.

00:11:12.047 --> 00:11:15.923
But, the main thing you learn is that we
have no moral advice to give to our kids.

00:11:15.947 --> 00:11:17.378
We have no moral shared norms.

00:11:17.402 --> 00:11:21.162
So, they're graduating from college.
They wonder, "What do I do with my life?"

00:11:21.186 --> 00:11:24.247
And we say, "Be free! Enjoy your freedom!"

00:11:24.271 --> 00:11:25.957
And that doesn't help them define.

00:11:25.981 --> 00:11:29.654
So then we say, "The future
is limitless, take risks."

00:11:29.678 --> 00:11:31.271
That doesn't help them choose.